NODE id=matrix/mcl/llm.DetectProvider kind=func
  digest=b3:2fcf74c4e2cded24c76e51dd4b15802f81f6c2daf34e4d7a164c27d1f4a4d7cf file=MCL/llm/llm.go range=799:828 lang=go exported=true byte_range=28048:29664
  sig=func DetectProvider(model string) (Provider, error)
  doc=DetectProvider maps a model string to its provider.\n\n	"accounts/fireworks/models/<X>"                 → Fireworks\n	"grok-*"                                         → xAI (Grok — primary chat provider)\n	"claude-*" / "gpt-5*" / opencode bare-model id  → Opencode (sess#34)\n	"<vendor>/<model>"                              → Baseten (fallback chat provider)\n\nGrok models ("grok-*", e.g. "grok-4.3") route to xAI's OpenAI-compatible API\n(api.x.ai). The bare "grok-*" id is both the fleet id (rate card, whitelists,\nenv pins) and xAI's native model code — no send-time rewrite is needed\n(unlike the retired Z.ai path). The xAI check precedes the opencode bare-id\ncheck so grok-build-* resolves to xAI rather than opencode. The remaining\ngeneric "<vendor>/<model>" shape resolves to Baseten. Together remains\nreachable but only when selected explicitly via Config.Provider + ProviderSet\n(it is the gateway alt-path, never auto-detected from a bare model id).
EDGES
  calls=matrix/mcl/llm.IsXaiModel,matrix/mcl/llm.IsXiaomiModel,matrix/mcl/llm.isOpencodeModelID
  references=matrix/mcl/llm.IsXaiModel,matrix/mcl/llm.IsXiaomiModel,matrix/mcl/llm.Provider,matrix/mcl/llm.ProviderBaseten,matrix/mcl/llm.ProviderFireworks,matrix/mcl/llm.ProviderOpencode,matrix/mcl/llm.ProviderXai,matrix/mcl/llm.ProviderXiaomi,matrix/mcl/llm.isOpencodeModelID,matrix/mcl/llm.model
  ^calls=matrix/mcl/llm.New,matrix/neo/internal/llm.New
  ^references=matrix/mcl/llm.New,matrix/neo/internal/llm.New
  ^defines=matrix/mcl/llm/llm.go

